              "expanded_url": "https://x.com/GraybeardWisdom/status/2121714279103578416/video/1",
              "media_key": "13_2121713321359405056",
              "start": 274,
              "url": "https://t.co/fTpyFGXGHd"
            }
          ]
        },
        "id": "2121714279103578416",
        "lang": "en",
        "note_tweet": {
          "text": "Robotaxi didn't come first. Supervised driving did. And most companies are rolling out AI in the opposite order.\n\nAutonomy only counts as a success if it's near perfect. Supervised AI just has to beat a person working alone. I think that gap is why AI is stalled in so many companies.\n\nIf my car is driving itself and I get pulled over, I get the ticket. I was supervising. I own it. That's the model I'd use for AI at work: arm the people doing the work, keep them accountable, and let what they do build what autonomy will need later.\n\nNine minutes on why we have it backwards."
        },
